    "lines": [
      {
        "scene": "hook",
        "text": "Marvel borrowed to make its own movies, and the security was Captain America.",
        "start": 0.3,
        "seconds": 3.07,
        "window": 3.73,
        "fill": 0.823
      },
      {
        "scene": "broke",
        "text": "The decade before, Marvel had gone bankrupt.",
        "start": 4.03,
        "seconds": 1.62,
        "window": 2.3,
        "fill": 0.704
      },
      {
        "scene": "rights",
        "text": "Its biggest heroes were out on licence: Spider-Man at Sony, the X-Men at Fox. So how could it make its own films?",
        "start": 6.33,
        "seconds": 5.54,
        "window": 6.2,
        "fill": 0.894
      },
      {
        "scene": "loan",
        "text": "So Marvel took a $525M credit line, arranged by Merrill Lynch.",
        "start": 12.53,
        "seconds": 4.05,
        "window": 4.73,
        "fill": 0.856
      },
      {
        "scene": "filing",
        "text": "Its filing says the film rights to 10 characters were pledged as collateral, Captain America and the Avengers among them.",
        "start": 17.27,
        "seconds": 5.04,
        "window": 5.7,
        "fill": 0.884
      },
      {
        "scene": "list",
        "text": "Black Panther and Doctor Strange were on the list too. So what would Marvel film first?",
        "start": 22.97,
        "seconds": 3.61,
        "window": 4.3,
        "fill": 0.84
      },
      {
        "scene": "ironman",
        "text": "Its first film was Iron Man, starring Robert Downey Junior, and that same loan paid for it.",
        "start": 27.27,
        "seconds": 3.79,
        "window": 4.4,
        "fill": 0.861
      },
      {
        "scene": "disney",
        "text": "Then Disney came, offering $30 a share in cash, plus stock, for more than 5,000 characters.",
        "start": 31.67,
        "seconds": 4.58,
        "window": 5.27,
        "fill": 0.869
      },
      {
        "scene": "payoff",
        "text": "In all, Disney agreed to pay about $4B for the company that had pledged its own heroes.",
        "start": 36.93,
        "seconds": 4.26,
        "window": 4.93,
        "fill": 0.864
      },
      {
        "scene": "ending",
        "text": "Iron Man or Captain America: which hero saved Marvel? Next time you see the Avengers, remember,",
        "start": 41.87,
        "seconds": 4.37,
        "window": 5.03,
        "fill": 0.869
      }
    ]
  },
